# VI. CODA  b117-126  (3/4, E-flat major)
# A single violin, muted orchestra: the sarabande's first phrase,
# now in the major (eb bb | c a-flat | g f eb | d | eb) over an E-flat
# pedal.  Then the last progression is plagal, with the minor
# subdominant as the final shadow: A-flat/E-flat -> A-flat minor/E-flat
# -> E-flat.  The line c - c-flat - b-flat (oboe above, cellos below)
# is the sarabande's lament bass in miniature, now consoled.
# The last sound: E-flat major, ppp, the third (g5) on top.

== b117-126 [R] ==
@ T=50 "Coda - Adagio, lontano"
@@ b117 T=50
@@ b118 T=50
@@ b119 T=48
@@ b120 T=45
@@ b121 T=48
@@ b122 T=46
@@ b123 T=41
@@ b124 T=40
@@ b125 T=37
@@ b126 T=22
vn1: | 2 {pp}{solo}{"semplice - like a memory"} [eb5 4 bb4 | 4 c5 2 ab5 | 4. g5 8 f5 4 eb5 | 2. d5 | 2. eb5] | R*2 | 2. {ppp}{tutti}{"lontano, sul tasto"} g5~ | 2. g5~ | 2. g5* |
vn2: | 2. {ppp}{"sul tasto, flautando"} g4 | 2. c5 | 2. bb4 | 2. ab4 | 2. g4 | R*2 | 2. {ppp} bb4~ | 2. bb4~ | 2. bb4* |
va:  | 2. {ppp}{"sul tasto, flautando"} eb4 | 2. eb4 | 2. eb4 | 2. f4 | 2. eb4 | R*2 | 2. {ppp} eb4~ | 2. eb4~ | 2. eb4* |
vc:  | 2. {ppp}{"sul tasto, flautando"} bb2 | 2. ab2 | 2. bb2 | 2. f2 | 2. g2 | 2. {pp} c3 | 2. cb3 | 2. {ppp} bb2~ | 2. bb2~ | 2. bb2* |
cb:  | 2. {ppp} eb2~ | 2. eb2~ | 2. eb2~ | 2. eb2~ | 2. eb2~ | 2. eb2~ | 2. eb2~ | 2. eb2~ | 2. eb2~ | 2. eb2* |
timp: | 2. {ppp}{"quasi niente"} eb2~=z | 2. eb2=z | R*5 | 2. {ppp} eb2~=z | 2. eb2~=z | 2. eb2=z |
ob:  | R*5 | 2. {pp}{"dolce"} [c5 | 2. cb5 | 2. {>} bb4~ | 2. {ppp} bb4] | R |
cl:  | R*5 | 2. {pp} ab4 | 2. ab4 | 2. {>} g4~ | 2. {ppp} g4 | R |
ca:  | R*5 | 2. {pp} eb4 | 2. eb4 | 2. {>} eb4~ | 2. {ppp} eb4 | R |
fg:  | R*5 | 2. {pp} ab2 | 2. ab2 | 2. {>} g2~ | 2. {ppp} g2 | R |

HANDOFF:
  END OF WORK.  Hold the final E-flat chord (fermata) until the sound is
  gone; then a silence as long as the chord.
